# nodeAddressAutodetectionV4.cidrs — restricts Calico to only the workload-VLAN interface (prevents
# it from picking the wrong NIC on a multi-NIC node — see docs/troubleshooting/networking-and-cni.md,
# Root cause B). Staged into manifests/ BEFORE rke2-server starts.
#
# `iptablesBackend` is deliberately NOT set here — it isn't actually a valid field on the
# Installation CRD (operator.tigera.io/v1); a strict-validating Calico chart version rejects it
# outright and CrashLoopBackOffs forever with an empty calico-system, while an older chart version
# just silently ignored it (which is why setting it through this exact path once had zero effect —
# a real no-op, not a timing/sync issue). If a Legacy iptables backend is ever genuinely needed, the
# correct approach is patching FelixConfiguration DIRECTLY, AFTER Calico is already installed — see
# 07-join-cluster.yml and docs/troubleshooting/networking-and-cni.md — not here.
apiVersion: helm.cattle.io/v1
kind: HelmChartConfig
metadata:
  name: rke2-calico
  namespace: kube-system
spec:
  valuesContent: |-
    installation:
      calicoNetwork:
        nodeAddressAutodetectionV4:
          cidrs:
            - "{{ calico_vm_cidr }}"
